group: D2h
formula: C2H4
construction: two equivalent halves
headline: 
note: Fragments: the two sides of C1–C2 · energies in Hartree · labels in D<sub>2h</sub> · 2 core orbitals hidden
about: **What is drawn.** The molecular levels in the middle are the calculation's own orbital energies, in Hartree.\n\n**Fragment levels.** Each fragment level is placed at the mean of the molecular orbitals it became, weighted by its share of them, and kept in the atom's own shell order. Its free-atom energy is given beside it.\n\n**Symmetry.** Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in D2h; the code reported none.\n\n**Not shown.** 2 core orbitals below −10.17 Hartree.\n\n**Picked atoms.** One atom is drawn against the atoms bonded to it; two bonded atoms cut that bond and the two sides are drawn against each other (in and out of phase when they are equal). A metal gives the fragment-orbital diagram, each ligand being a connected piece left when the metal is removed.
